    "statementHTML": "<div class=\"statement-body\">\n<div class=\"statement-section statement-goal\">\n   <h2><span class=\"icon icon-goal\">&nbsp;</span><span>Goal </span></h2>\n   <span class=\"question-statement\">Every number hides a rotation instruction in its binary representation.<br><br>Given a positive integer <var>N</var>, perform the following steps:<br><br>1. Convert <var>N</var> to binary without leading zeros.<br>2. Count the number of bits equal to <const>1</const>.<br>3. Rotate the binary digits circularly to the <strong>left</strong> by that number of positions.<br>4. Convert the rotated binary sequence back to decimal.<br>5. Output the <strong>bitwise XOR</strong> of the original number and the rotated number.<br><br><strong>Circular rotation:</strong> Bits leaving the left end reappear on the right. The binary sequence keeps its original length, including any leading zeros created during rotation.<br><br><strong>XOR:</strong> Two bits produce <const>1</const> if they are different, otherwise <const>0</const>.<br><br><strong>Example:</strong><br><br><var>N</var> = <const>13</const><br><br>Binary: <const>1101</const><br><br>Number of <const>1</const> bits: <const>3</const><br><br>Rotate left <const>3</const> times:<br><br><const>1101</const> -&gt; <const>1011</const> -&gt; <const>0111</const> -&gt; <const>1110</const><br><br>XOR:<br><br><const>1101</const> XOR <const>1110</const> = <const>0011</const><br><br>Result: <const>3</const><br><br>Can you solve it using as little code as possible?</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"statement-section statement-protocol\">\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Input</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-input\"><strong>Line 1:</strong> A positive integer <var>N</var>.</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Output</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-output\"><strong>Line 1:</strong> An integer: the bitwise XOR of <var>N</var> and its circularly left-rotated binary representation, expressed in decimal.</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Constraints</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-constraints\"><const>1</const> &le; <var>N</var> &le; <const>10⁹</const></div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Example</div>\n      <div class=\"statement-inout\">\n         <div class=\"statement-inout-in\">\n            <div class=\"title\">Input</div>\n            <pre class=\"question-statement-example-in\">13</pre>\n         </div>\n         <div class=\"statement-inout-out\">\n            <div class=\"title\">Output</div>\n            <pre class=\"question-statement-example-out\">3</pre>\n         </div>\n      </div>\n   </div>\n</div>"
